{"id": "EUVD-2026-71294", "enisaUuid": "9811744f-4bd5-33ff-b016-6e5254f61893", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: ah6: validate routing header segments_left\n\nAH6 rearranges routing-header addresses before computing or verifying the\nICV. ipv6_rearrange_rthdr() assumes that segments_left is not larger than\nthe number of addresses described by the routing header's hdrlen field.\n\nThat assumption does not hold for raw IPv6 HDRINCL packets. A packet with\nhdrlen equal to 2 describes one address, but can carry an arbitrary\nsegments_left value. With segments_left equal to 255, the function moves\nits address pointer 4,064 bytes backwards and passes a 4,064-byte length to\nmemmove(), resulting in an out-of-bounds access.\n\nValidate the invariant locally before modifying the routing header or\nperforming any address-pointer arithmetic, and propagate malformed-header\nerrors to the existing AH6 input and output error paths.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2dc650956e4e163b879b3fb1027f9557abc5c985", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48b0e36cf54358276ee7aa897034c973097d2bc9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b7e066eabcc7d6d8f476c34739b45932f2f4c31", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f00df8500e5a36ba70d336fd34bd2152ea074e5f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1516e31ac458a738be485620579d8f7fb2700fcb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6733ae71268a27d598cfb3f3339a3c950b9b656d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0bf11081ad3753938a2b48723ce6298dbac743a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46640c814f25f096b0b0045ca50e1b7030cd8a30", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bad4bda74dc4713f398d3b7624ff05478e3a568"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80844", "GHSA-jv4j-682x-84w7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "088b01c9-4b2a-310a-a576-562579dbbd65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.269"}, {"id": "2518d2f4-2803-3d0d-9718-07356d87bfae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.187"}, {"id": "5322c18a-5c37-346b-a3a5-7455f0068765", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <48b0e36cf54358276ee7aa897034c973097d2bc9"}, {"id": "537879b4-9875-3139-8c50-199dca207c39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <1516e31ac458a738be485620579d8f7fb2700fcb"}, {"id": "53fce17f-dc2d-38f4-84b5-b521fccc5acd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.13"}, {"id": "6308fce5-b954-30e3-bdb8-67a2540e5d7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.156"}, {"id": "6a95cae5-37e6-323a-a21c-b33cc8da6f40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <2dc650956e4e163b879b3fb1027f9557abc5c985"}, {"id": "8c54e8ae-3d86-3693-afe3-51334c7cebdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "9477abde-befb-3e8d-8e3b-62e5cc0471e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "94ef18b3-3e38-38ee-8dee-82cf36cf013c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <7bad4bda74dc4713f398d3b7624ff05478e3a568"}, {"id": "99da5501-79b2-3689-999c-b6f253ff43fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <1b7e066eabcc7d6d8f476c34739b45932f2f4c31"}, {"id": "9dd8c9ea-810f-374b-9892-573ed0409bfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.220"}, {"id": "a42e4e3e-ba6c-3efe-bde0-647a3a3602